    "result_text": "I've implemented `draft_reply` in `app/drafts.py`. The two existing `suggest_tag` tests still pass, but no test calls `draft_reply` yet. I tried a quick check against a fake client and the environment's permission settings blocked running inline Python, so the new function hasn't been run at all.\n\nIt makes the same kind of call as `suggest_tag`: model `DRAFT_MODEL`, `STYLE_GUIDE` as the instructions, and the subject and body as the input. It caps output at `MAX_DRAFT_TOKENS`, sets `store=False`, and sends `metadata={\"ticket_id\": ticket.id}`. It returns a `Draft` with the ticket id and the reply text with surrounding whitespace stripped.\n\n**When a reply counts as truncated:** only when the response's status is `\"incomplete\"` and the reason given is `\"max_output_tokens\"`. If the reply stops for another reason, such as a content filter, `truncated` stays False, as you asked.\n\n**Checking the API:** the project notes say to look up library APIs with Context7 first, but its monthly quota was used up. I checked the installed `openai==3.19.2` package source instead. `responses.create` accepts `metadata`, `store` and `max_output_tokens`, and `\"max_output_tokens\"` is one of the possible reasons a response is marked incomplete.\n\nIf you want, I can add tests for the full, truncated and content-filter cases to `tests/`, using the same fake-client pattern as `test_tags.py`."
